Z||000001||ChadMan||12-17-1999||09:28 AM||||Hard to say without seeing the car - I'm guessing no less than $1500 and no more than $2500, unless the car's in near-perfect condition.<P>I just got $1700 for my 86 SE 4-sp.  It looked good and ran strong, but the steering was kind of sloppy (tie rod ends?) and the clutch was in advancing middle age.  But I sure wish I hadn't sold it.||||reg||1
